  "id": "attachment-behavior",
  "term": "attachment behavior",
  "definition": "Attachment behavior is the pattern of responses shown in relation to a primary attachment figure, especially how an individual reacts to that figure’s presence versus separation. In this source, it refers to behaviors linked to close social bonding that begin in infancy and can remain associated with social behavior in adulthood.",
